<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29999" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūnĭfĭcentĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f.
		munificus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>bountifulness, munificence, liberality,
			generosity</i> (class., but not in Cic. or Cæs.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caesar beneficiis ac munificentiā
					magnus habebatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. C. 54, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caesaris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naturae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					27, 1, 1, § 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liberalitatem et munificentiam exercere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					39, 5, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
